      "summary": "langfuse-loop.sh: send unsent turns to Langfuse as they appear",
      "body": "sync.py langfuse gains --pending (sessions whose latest stored log has turns not yet sent; a state-file mark by log sha keeps the check cheap) and --all (send them). llm-dlc/tools/langfuse-loop.sh polls that list, runs --all, retries while Langfuse is down, and takes stop/now/? commands like verification-loop.sh, with no Claude session. Verified against the local Langfuse: 19 pending sessions sent, then the loop idles on 'nothing to send'.",
